Objective: Determine the most effective approach for regenerating historical data in the Radar Data Model from cost, speed, and operational control perspectives.

Key Question: Should we process data day-by-day (all notebooks for 1 day) or monthly (1 notebook for entire month)?

Scope:

15-20 datasets
15-20 million records per dataset per day
Target: Full month historical backfill (30+ days)
Estimated total: 300-400 million records per dataset per month
Current Approach
Method: 1 type of object for entire month at once
Challenge: Need to evaluate if day-by-day approach would be faster or more cost-effective
Cluster Options:
Single-node (DAB-small): No data shuffling, 32GB RAM, driver-only
High-end multi-node (DAB-large): 128GB RAM per node, 2-4 workers, Photon-enabled
Medium autoscale (DAB-medium): 64GB RAM per node, 2-4 workers
Business Value
Cost optimization: Reduce compute expenses for historical data regeneration
Time efficiency: Minimize total processing time for backfills
Operational control: Better granularity for monitoring and failure recovery
